      "id": "sign-and-commit",
      "description": "Canonicalise the record without its signature (object keys sorted by code point, no whitespace, strings, booleans and safe integers only), sign SHA-256 of those bytes with the BRC-42 child of the custodian key for protocol [1, \"dpp managed record v1\"], key identifier requestId and counterparty anyone (the BRC-100 createSignature operation), then canonicalise the signed record and hash it: that digest is what the UPDATE or RETIRE carries in field 15 (spec managed-custody.md section 6).",
